WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.970
This is Knoxville Flooring's application,
built by Catalyst

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.450
Innovations. We are using sample
information to show how room measurements

3
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.910
become an estimate. Start by choosing a
room and entering its length

4
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.390
and width. The estimator calculates the
floor area, keeping the measurements

5
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.870
and the quantity together. Next, review
the assumptions around the

6
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.230
work. Waste allowance, material costs, and
labor all affect

7
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.670
the estimate. Preparation matters too.

8
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.750
The application includes options for work
such as tear-out and subfloor

9
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.250
repair, so those details can be considered
alongside the flooring itself.

10
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.590
As the inputs change, review the updated
summary.

11
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.250
It brings the quantity, entered costs,
suggested price, and

12
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.470
estimated margin into one view.

13
00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.030
These are sample calculations, not a
promise of profit.

14
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.090
Finally, the proposal handoff provides a
next step from the estimate.

15
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:59.210
We are stopping before creating or sending
anything to a customer.

16
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.270
Measurements, job details, and pricing
stay connected.

17
00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:07.370
Talk with Catalyst about building software
around the way your team estimates

18
00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.790
and manages work.

